    {
      "id": "delegation",
      "hidden": false,
      "layout": "auto",
      "background": null,
      "header": "",
      "aside": "",
      "speaker": "",
      "print": "",
      "steps": 3,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "title",
          "content": "3. AI in government",
          "step": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "start": 1,
          "progressive": true,
          "size": "normal",
          "items": [
            {
              "content": "**It starts small.** Benefit claims, permits, tax audits.",
              "step": 0
            },
            {
              "content": "**It will not stay small.** Budgets, policing, who gets what.",
              "step": 1
            },
            {
              "content": "**Tight budgets will force it.** A model is cheaper than a civil servant.",
              "step": 2
            }
          ],
          "step": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "size": "normal",
          "content": "**They will need people** to study, evaluate and implement it.",
          "step": 3,
          "align": "center"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "size": "normal",
          "content": "*Ministries · Parliaments · Audit offices · EU AI Office*",
          "step": 3,
          "align": "center"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "size": "tiny",
          "content": "On delegation: Epstein and O'Halloran (1999). Huber and Shipan (2002).",
          "step": 0
        }
      ]
    },
